From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:25:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: shm: reallocate the draw buffer when it has to grow

lv_wayland_shm_resize_window() resizes the LVGL draw buffer with
lv_draw_buf_reshape(), which fails when the buffer is too small for the
new size and returns NULL. The window then has no draw buffer and LVGL
only logs "No draw buffer" on every refresh, so nothing is ever drawn.

This happens whenever the compositor configures the surface larger than
the size passed to lv_wayland_window_create(), e.g. right at startup
under Weston's kiosk shell or after a fullscreen request.

Allocate a new draw buffer of the required size in that case and hand
it to the display.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [v9.4.x only; the Wayland driver was reworked for v9.5]
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@gmail.com>
---
 src/drivers/wayland/lv_wl_shm.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/wayland/lv_wl_shm.c b/src/drivers/wayland/lv_wl_shm.c
index 5d479b0..43872f7 100644
--- a/src/drivers/wayland/lv_wl_shm.c
+++ b/src/drivers/wayland/lv_wl_shm.c
@@ -156,9 +156,31 @@ lv_result_t lv_wayland_shm_resize_window(shm_ctx_t * context, struct window * wi
 
     if(window->lv_disp != NULL) {
         /* Resize draw buffer */
-        const uint32_t stride = lv_draw_buf_width_to_stride(width, lv_display_get_color_format(window->lv_disp));
-        window->lv_draw_buf = lv_draw_buf_reshape(window->lv_draw_buf, lv_display_get_color_format(window->lv_disp),
-                                                  width, height / LVGL_DRAW_BUFFER_DIV, stride);
+        const lv_color_format_t cf = lv_display_get_color_format(window->lv_disp);
+        const uint32_t stride = lv_draw_buf_width_to_stride(width, cf);
+        lv_draw_buf_t * draw_buf = lv_draw_buf_reshape(window->lv_draw_buf, cf, width,
+                                                       height / LVGL_DRAW_BUFFER_DIV, stride);
+
+        if(draw_buf == NULL) {
+            /* Reshaping cannot grow the buffer, e.g. when the compositor
+             * configures a fullscreen surface larger than the requested
+             * window size. Replace it with a buffer of the new size. */
+            lv_draw_buf_t * old_buf = window->lv_draw_buf;
+
+            draw_buf = lv_draw_buf_create(width, height / LVGL_DRAW_BUFFER_DIV, cf, stride);
+            if(draw_buf == NULL) {
+                LV_LOG_ERROR("Cannot allocate a %dx%d draw buffer", width, height);
+                return LV_RESULT_INVALID;
+            }
+            /* At startup lv_wayland_window_create() attaches
+             * window->lv_draw_buf once the surface is configured; later
+             * the display still uses the old buffer, so replace it there. */
+            if(window->is_window_configured) {
+                lv_display_set_draw_buffers(window->lv_disp, draw_buf, NULL);
+            }
+            if(old_buf) lv_draw_buf_destroy(old_buf);
+        }
+        window->lv_draw_buf = draw_buf;
     }
 
     return LV_RESULT_OK;
-- 
